.Dd May 28, 2026
.Dt XTC_PDICT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_pdict_put ,
.Nm xtc_pdict_put_with_dtor ,
.Nm xtc_pdict_get ,
.Nm xtc_pdict_erase ,
.Nm xtc_pdict_count ,
.Nm xtc_pdict_clear
.Nd Erlang-style per-process dictionary
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.In xtc_pdict.h
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_pdict_put "const char *key" "void *value"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_pdict_put_with_dtor "const char *key" "void *value" "xtc_pdict_dtor_fn dtor"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_pdict_get "const char *key" "void **value"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_pdict_erase "const char *key"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_pdict_count "void"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_pdict_clear "void"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm xtc_pdict
is a per-process dictionary similar to Erlang's
.Sq put/get/erase .
Each
.Xr xtc_proc 3
has its own private key-value store.
When the proc exits, however it exits, its remaining entries are
removed after its
.Fn xtc_proc_at_exit
hooks have run, and each entry's destructor, if it has one, is invoked
on its value.
A proc still alive when its loop is finalized has its entries
removed by
.Fn xtc_loop_destroy
.Pq see Xr xtc_loop 3
the same way; there the destructors run on the thread calling
.Fn xtc_loop_destroy ,
not on the proc.
.Pp
The store lives in a side-table keyed by pid rather than embedded
in the proc struct, so adding a pdict entry doesn't affect the
in-struct fast path.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_pdict_put
binds
.Fa key
to
.Fa value
in the calling proc's dictionary.
.Fn xtc_pdict_put_with_dtor
is the same but takes a
.Fa dtor
callback.  If
.Fa dtor
is non-NULL, it's invoked with the prior value
.Pq if any
when the entry is replaced or erased, and on every entry when the
proc exits.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_pdict_get
stores the current value of
.Fa key
in
.Fa *value .
.Pp
.Fn xtc_pdict_erase
removes the entry, invoking the dtor if registered.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_pdict_count
returns the number of entries in the calling proc's dictionary;
.Fn xtc_pdict_clear
removes them all, invoking each registered dtor.
.Pp
Destructors run with the dictionary's internal lock held, so a
destructor must not call any
.Fn xtc_pdict_*
function.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xtc_pdict_put ,
.Fn xtc_pdict_put_with_dtor ,
.Fn xtc_pdict_get ,
.Fn xtc_pdict_erase
and
.Fn xtc_pdict_clear
return
.Dv XTC_OK
on success and
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL
when called outside a proc, for a NULL argument, or (get and erase)
when
.Fa key
is absent.
The puts return
.Dv XTC_E_NOMEM
when an entry cannot be allocated.
.Fn xtc_pdict_count
returns the number of entries, 0 outside a proc.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static void my_dtor(void *p) { free(p); }

/* Stash a per-request scratch buffer in the dict. */
char *buf = malloc(4096);
xtc_pdict_put_with_dtor("scratch", buf, my_dtor);

/* Later in the same proc... */
void *b;
if (xtc_pdict_get("scratch", &b) == XTC_OK)
        use(b);
/* No clear needed: my_dtor frees buf when the proc exits. */
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_loop 3 ,
.Xr xtc_proc 3 ,
.Xr xtc_mctx 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
.Sh HISTORY
Appeared in xtc 0.1.
